st's s.ctx, while confirm deletes the earlier queue entry and pendingReadIndex.addReady requires an exact SystemCtx key. The sequential control confirms the same consumer path with node 2's admitted context first: its reply carries that context and completion is 1 with batch index 4. The logical-deadline case keeps the later-first ordering: its event 1 records original_batch_index zero, no completion before the 50-tick deadline, RequestTimeout at advanced tick 51, and the stale batch absent after GC. Together these distinguish a context-association defect from a general consumer or harness failure and measure the bounded client endpoint. The main reply's log index is a later committed index, so no stale-read value or safety violation is established. The request remains uncompleted after a valid applied index until the measured logical timeout.\",\n      \"knowledge\": [\n        {\n          \"entry_id\": \"827f420be72d403f9a804a543fac77cc-knowledge-0\",\n          \"revision\": 1,\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
